Stadium in Cardiff. It starts on 11 December, but the boxers will fight early on 12 December. The most expensive ticket cost £13,128. The cheapest was £88.50. More than 500,000 people waited online to buy tickets. Soon after, people sold tickets on other websites. One VIP seat near the ring was advertised for £73,645. Netflix will show the fight around the world. Fury is 38 and Joshua is 36. Both men were world champions two times. They will share about $200m. The undercard fights are not confirmed yet. The stadium will stay open until 03:30. The boxers will walk to the ring at about 01:00. A short music show comes first.", "vocab": [{"word": "ticket", "pos": "noun", "zh": "票", "note": "买票、卖票都用这个词"}, {"word": "sell out", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "卖光", "note": "票卖完时常用"}, {"word": "fight", "pos": "noun", "zh": "比赛；打斗", "note": "拳击比赛常用"}, {"word": "expensive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "贵的", "note": "反义词是 cheap"}, {"word": "cheap", "pos": "adj", "zh": "便宜的", "note": "反义词是 expensive"}, {"word": "online", "pos": "adv", "zh": "在网上", "note": "常和 buy、wait 一起用"}, {"word": "champion", "pos": "noun", "zh": "冠军", "note": "world champion 世界冠军"}, {"word": "stadium", "pos": "noun", "zh": "体育场", "note": "看比赛的地方"}], "title_original": "Fury-Joshua tickets priced up to £13,000 sell out in one hour", "summary_original": "Tickets for Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua's fight at Cardiff's Principality Stadium sells out in just one hour.", "body_original": "Fury-Joshua tickets priced up to £13,000 sell out in one hour\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nTickets for Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua's fight at Cardiff's Principality Stadium have sold out in just one hour.\nFury and Joshua will meet on a bill that begins on 11 December but they are not expected to fight until the early hours of 12 December.\nThe highest-priced tickets were available at £13,128, including booking fees, with the lowest at £88.50.\nThe all-British heavyweight contest, which will be broadcast globally on Netflix, was\nannounced in September\nand around 80,000 tickets went on sale at 12:00 BST on Friday.\nJust minutes after the tickets went on sale more than 500,000 people were waiting in the online queue.\nTickets quickly began emerging on resale websites, with ringside VIP seats being advertised for £73,645, while upper tier seats were available for £425.\nRingwalks are\nexpected to start around 01:00 GMT\non Saturday 12 December, following a short live music performance, and the stadium will remain open until 03:30.\nThe event is being promoted as a collaboration between Saudi boxing powerbroker Turki Alalshikh's The Ring and UFC chief Dana White.\nOrganisers are yet to confirm any of the undercard fights.\nWhat information do we collect from this quiz?\nJoshua, 36, and Fury, 38 - both former two-time world champions - signed contracts for the bout earlier this year, but the date and venue had yet to be confirmed.\nLondon's Wembley Stadium and New York's Madison Square Garden were the frontrunners to stage the fight, but both presented issues before Cardiff emerged as an alternative.\nThe Principality Stadium has hosted late-night boxing before, including Joe Calzaghe's fight with Mikkel Kessler in November 2007, which began at 01:00 GMT.\nRicky Hatton's victory over Kostya Tszyu at Manchester's MEN Arena in 2005 began at about 02:00 local time, allowing US broadcaster Showtime to show the fight on Saturday evening.\nJust 11 days ago, there was uncertainty over whether the fight would even take place due to a dispute over the role of UFC chief White in the promotion of the event.\nBroadcaster Netflix said Alalshikh's The Ring and White would collaborate to promote the event, but Joshua's promoter Eddie Hearn said his fighter's contract prevented White from having a promotional role.\nThe British rivals finally met at a news conference on 30 September to begin the build-up to one of the most anticipated fights in British history.\nFury and Joshua are reported to be sharing a purse worth close to $200m (£151m)\nRelated topics\nBoxing\nBoxing schedule and results 2026\nPublished\n1 day ago\nWatch every Born to Brawl episode\nPublished\n28 April 2024\nMore boxing from the BBC\nNotifications, social media and more with BBC Sport\nPublished\n28 August", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:08:30.325164", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.287, "sm": 100, "em": 287, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "fight", "s": 0.3, "e": 0.65, "sm": 300, "em": 649, "cs": 4, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "is", "s": 0.662, "e": 0.75, "sm": 662, "em": 750, "cs": 10, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "at", "s": 0.762, "e": 0.862, "sm": 762, "em": 862, "cs": 13, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "the", "s": 0.875, "e": 0.963, "sm": 875, "em": 962, "cs": 16, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Principality", "s": 0.975, "e": 1.688, "sm": 975, "em": 1687, "cs": 20, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "Stadium", "s": 1.7, "e": 2.175, "sm": 1700, "em": 2175, "cs": 33, "ce": 40, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "in", "s": 2.188, "e": 2.3, "sm": 2187, "em": 2300, "cs": 41, "ce": 43, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "Cardiff", "s": 2.312, "e": 2.875, "sm": 2312, "em": 2875, "cs": 44, "ce": 51, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": ".", "s": 2.875, "e": 3.737, "sm": 2875, "em": 3737, "cs": 51, "ce": 52, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "It", "s": 3.737, "e": 3.925, "sm": 3737, "em": 3925, "cs": 53, "ce": 55, "si": 1}, {"i": 11, "w": "starts", "s": 3.938, "e": 4.312, "sm": 3937, "em": 4312, "cs": 56, "ce": 62, "si": 1}, {"i": 12, "w": "on", "s": 4.325, "e": 4.45, "sm": 4325, "em": 4450, "cs": 63, "ce": 65, "si": 1}, {"i": 13, "w": "11", "s": 4.463, "e": 4.65, "sm": 4462, "em": 4650, "cs": 66, "ce": 68, "si": 1}, {"i": 14, "w": "December", "s": 4.65, "e": 5.4, "sm": 4650, "em": 5400, "cs": 69, "ce": 77, "si": 1}, {"i": 15, "w": ",", "s": 5.4, "e": 5.675, "sm": 5400, "em": 5675, "cs": 77, "ce": 78, "si": 1}, {"i": 16, "w": "but", "s": 5.675, "e": 5.812, "sm": 5675, "em": 5812, "cs": 79, "ce": 82, "si": 1}, {"i": 17